operator_ruling_verbatim.text:
Choose (a): close external corpus review round 1 on the pinned-tool re-check.

Record the following ruling.

The round-1 corpus review may close now because all review-stage requirements that can exist under the frozen ordering have been satisfied:

- all repaired fixtures completed the required re-adjudication;
- every MUST-FIX finding from Reviewers A and B is resolved;
- required disclosures and errata are recorded and bound;
- the complete 26-fix corpus passes the frozen checks;
- the pinned independence tool that produced the frozen values reproduces all required values with 0 violations;
- the historical and sealed artifacts remain unchanged except for the explicitly authorized O2 disclosure append.

The forked-module re-check is not a corpus-review closure prerequisite because "g_route4_independence" does not yet exist and, under the frozen design, is created during the subsequent implementation stage.

Do not implement the module merely to close round 1, and do not reverse the frozen ordering.

Instead, carry B7 forward unchanged as a mandatory freeze condition:

«After "g_route4_independence" is implemented from the frozen design, the final pre-freeze independence re-check using that forked module must reproduce the required frozen values and satisfy the same bounds. Failure of that check blocks freeze and cannot be waived by the successful pinned-tool result.»

The successful pinned-tool reproduction is evidence that the reviewed 26-fix corpus currently satisfies the frozen independence requirements. It is not a substitute for the later forked-module qualification.

Close external corpus review round 1 and bind this ruling into the closure record.

The next stage is implementation under frozen design step 4. Do not begin implementation until separately authorized.

Preserve all current integrity boundaries:

- no modification of sealed historical artifacts;
- no movement of "main", "g-route4/seal", or the frozen tag as part of review closure;
- no reinterpretation of completed adjudication;
- no weakening of B7 or any other freeze criterion.
